# Everything VIDE ships is text that executes or is byte-compared on Linux.
# Pin LF at the git layer so a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) cannot
# smuggle CRLF into the bash shims (install.sh, vide, tests/*.sh) or into
# files the parity tier byte-compares. The repo tracks no binaries today;
# if one ever lands, mark it `-text` here explicitly.
* text=auto eol=lf
